'' AN ESCAPED LITERAL REACHED __FB_EVAL__ UNDECODED, and it refused every one.
''
'' The preprocessor reads a RAW SOURCE SPAN, so a backslash escape had not been
'' decoded; '#if' compares content and had always been content with that, but
'' __FB_EVAL__ has to RE-EMIT the value and undecoded bytes are a different string. So
'' it declined -- '!"plain"' included, which has no escape in it at all -- and every
'' USE of the result declined with it. pp/macro-eval-str.bas is 11 of those and its
'' utf16le twin another 11.
''
'' The decoder is now shared with MIR's own literal reader rather than written twice:
'' Tko.Text.DecodeEscapedBody, gated by check-escape's 52 measured answers.
''
'' A WIDE result still declines. It re-emits as '!"\uXXXX"' per character -- measured,
'' __FB_EVAL__( wstr( "A" ) ) is 'A' -- and the preprocessor has no wide value to
'' render. That is 6 of the 11 in each of those two files, and they stay open.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/eval-escaped-string.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' EXPECT-OUT: "plain"
'' GOLDEN: expected/eval-escaped-string.out
